new file mode 100644
index 0000000..40f6046
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/caller-admission-pilot.md
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# Optional caller admission pilot
+
+This proposal adds provider-neutral hooks. It adds no Aithos dependency, default
+network call, or changed admission policy when the hooks are omitted.
+
+Pass the **same object** as `callerAccess` to `createSalesAgentHarnessApp` and as
+`admission` to `createSalesAgentHttpHandler`. Its request scope must be established
+before invoking the handler callback. Never derive `TrustedCaller` from request
+JSON or an unverified identity/session header.
+
+The implementation must verify identity, evaluate policy and durably reserve audit
+events before it calls the runtime or commerce tools. `allows` is enforced for
+model-selected tools as well as direct commerce requests; merchant policy still
+applies afterwards. `aroundSession` and `aroundAction` instrument outcomes without
+receiving message text, tokens, product details or customer data.
+
+Session ownership is persisted with session creation in all built-in stores.
+Existing ownerless sessions are **not** automatically adopted. Duplicate session
+IDs cannot replace a previous owner's record, including expired records. Clients
+must create a fresh session after expiry. Commerce context remains server-only.
+In admission mode, external session creation cannot inject a Shopware context
+token, customer context or non-A2A channel. The SQLite migration adds a nullable
+column and preserves existing rows; existing SQLite installations should be backed
+up before migration as usual. File stores now validate persisted session fields.
+
+Agent Card extensions are supplied by the admission implementation. Request body
+debug logging is disabled while admission is active. This hook does not implement
+an A2A client, replace the runtime, or expand this harness's synchronous A2A binding.
+Long tasks, streaming, checkout and a real Shopware/LLM exercise are outside the
+synthetic Aithos identity pilot.
+
+The generic contract and session-store tests need no provider. The complementary
+Aithos repository contains an end-to-end fixture with a deterministic runtime and
+fake commerce adapter. No upstream PR or new package publication is implied by
+this local proposal.
